{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"close","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC5closeyyYaKF","title":"close()","role":"symbol"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"close"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Releases the HTTP client and its connection pool, and clears the cookie jar, the CSRF token"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and any retained "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/Sensitive","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" challenge token (§18.1 rule 6)."}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Idempotent","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (rule 2): calling it twice is a no-op the second time. Cleanup code runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from error paths, and an error path that itself throws hides the original failure."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does not log out"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" (rule 5): it issues no request. The server-side session deliberately"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"outlives the client object — that is what lets a process restart and resume — so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close()"},{"type":"text","text":" that logged out would silently end every user’s session on each deploy."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use after close is an error, not undefined","type":"text"}]},{"text":" (rule 4): every operation afterwards","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkError"},{"text":" naming the cause rather than silently reopening.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":", and releasing an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncHTTPClient"},{"type":"text","text":" is async, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this SDK cannot make deallocation a complete shutdown the way §18.1 rule 1’s “a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plus explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close()"},{"type":"text","text":"” suggests. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close()"},{"type":"text","text":" is therefore the only complete form, and is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stated as required rather than implied."}]}],"style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Deterministic shutdown (CONTRACT.md §18).","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/close()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/close()"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/docume